                'The best single sentence about work is also hers: I like feeling a little anxietal, a little scared, a little out of my depth every day. Out of my depth is swimming — past the point where your feet touch — and it is the most exact phrase English has for the good kind of fear. Wyle answers with the counterpart, which is what the fear costs: I make my wife stay up very late running lines with me, so I can go to work the next day and seem like I make it look effortless. Make it look effortless is the whole profession in four words, and the sentence before it is the invoice.',
