                'This summer Donna walked over at seven in the morning, held out a clipboard and said, “Sign people in. We are already behind.” Then she left, because Donna does not do ceremonies and had twelve other things to be behind on.',
                'Tommy signed people in for six hours. He did not sit down. He did not drink anything either, because you cannot hold a cup and a clipboard at the same time, and he was not putting the clipboard down.',
                'That clipboard is now in a frame in his hallway, at eye level, on the wall every guest has to pass on the way to the bathroom. When somebody asks about it he says, “Oh, that? That’s nothing.” Then he stands there. He can stand there a long time.',
                '— Donna keeps twenty years of clipboards in a box in her garage, sorted by year. She has never noticed that one of them is missing.',
