                'On the thirtieth it rained, and Daniel waited at the window of number twelve like a man who had lent out his own life and was watching to see it returned.',
                'The taxi came first. A woman got out — thin, older than her photographs, looking up at the building as if it might bite. Elena stood on the pavement a long moment and did not go to the door. She had run from this street once. She was not sure she could walk back onto it.',
                'Then, from the other end of the road, a man with a suitcase and a folded map, checking the numbers on the doors. Nine. Ten. Eleven. Tomas looked up, and saw her, and stopped — and the suitcase slipped out of his hand and stood forgotten in the rain, and neither of them moved, because after a year some distances have to be crossed slowly or not at all.',
