                'Halloran turned. The lamp of the dead tower swung its beam through the window and, for one deliberate instant, lit the foot of the stairs, where a boy of twelve stood dripping seawater onto the boards, exactly as he had been the morning they pulled him from the surf. The boy looked up. He was not frightened. He was only waiting, as he had waited thirty years, for his brother to stop saying not yet.',
                'And Halloran opened his mouth, and the tower held its breath, and the beam swung back out over the black and patient water.',
