                'The clip is about pub banter, which is the thing this newspaper keeps circling. Banter is hours of talk with no information in it, conducted with people you are not related to, for no purpose whatsoever, and it is the single hardest English there is to follow. There is no signposting. Nobody says the topic. The joke is usually a callback to something said forty minutes ago by someone who has since gone to the toilet. You can hold a C2 certificate and be completely locked out of it.',
                'Lock died of cancer in August 2021, aged fifty-eight. He had been a team captain on 8 Out of 10 Cats since 2005 and on Does Countdown since 2012 — a job that consists entirely of talking rubbish with the same people for fifteen years, which is to say, the healthiest job in the country by Hari’s standard.',
